OL,3,GNEWSABristol Greens leader opposes
OL,4,Aanti-Zionism vote
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe leader of a Green Party-run city
OL,7,Fcouncil has declared his opposition to
OL,8,Fa motion adopted by the national party
OL,9,Fdeclaring Zionism a form of racism.
OL,11,FOn Sunday during the Green Party
OL,12,Fconference, members passed a motion
OL,13,Fwhich defined Zionism as an ideology
OL,14,Fsupporting "an ethnonationalist Jewish
OL,15,Fstate".
OL,17,FBristol City Council leader Tony Dyer
OL,18,Fsaid he feels "compelled to speak up on
OL,19,Fa personal level and on behalf of the
OL,20,Fcouncil, to express my opposition".
OL,21,FCheltenham MP Max Wilkinson has also
OL,22,Fcriticised the vote.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
